    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Practice: Script Your Own Ackerman Ladder",
     "content": "Choose an upcoming negotiation in your own life — a salary discussion, a freelance rate, a car or furniture purchase, a vendor contract. Before any conversation happens, write down your genuine target number, the outcome you would consider a real win, and be honest with yourself about it rather than picking an aspirational fantasy figure. Calculate four figures from it: 65 percent, 85 percent, 95 percent, and a precise version of 100 percent that avoids round numbers (adjust the exact final figure slightly so it looks calculated rather than convenient — a few dollars or a small percentage point either direction is enough). Write all four numbers down on paper or in a note before you begin — the entire value of the method comes from not improvising the sequence under real-time pressure, when the temptation to skip straight to a comfortable middle number is strongest. Then identify one non-cash item you could attach to your final offer: extra time, an included extra, a faster timeline, a small service thrown in, something the other side values that costs you little relative to a further price cut. When the actual negotiation happens, resist the urge to skip straight to your target number even if you're tempted to soften the opening anchor — the extreme first offer and the shrinking increments that follow are doing real psychological work that a single reasonable-sounding offer cannot replicate on its own, no matter how fair that single number might actually be.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Practice: Script Your Own Ladder</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Four numbers, written down before you speak</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\">Step 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Name your real target number for an upcoming negotiation.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"450\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\">Step 2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"492\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Calculate 65%, 85%, 95%, and a precise 100% figure in advance.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"620\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"670\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\">Step 3</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"712\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Choose one non-cash item to attach to your final offer.</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"860\" width=\"900\" height=\"90\" rx=\"45\" fill=\"#ec4899\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"913\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Write all four numbers down — improvised ladders collapse under pressure</text></svg></svg>",
      "caption": "Plan all four offers before the conversation begins"
     }
    }
